1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,880
Welcome to Algebra One. Before we solve a
single equation, we need to know what

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:07,104
kinds of numbers we're working with.

3
00:00:07,554 --> 00:00:12,233
In this lesson, we'll sort numbers into
families, and see where every one of them

4
00:00:12,233 --> 00:00:13,677
lives on the number line.

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:19,801
Let's start with the numbers you first
learned: one, two, three, and so on.

6
00:00:20,251 --> 00:00:23,878
These are the natural numbers, also called
counting numbers.

7
00:00:24,328 --> 00:00:27,293
Add zero to that list, and you get the
whole numbers.

8
00:00:28,433 --> 00:00:33,191
Now include the negatives: negative one,
negative two, negative three.

9
00:00:33,641 --> 00:00:36,542
Together with the whole numbers, they make
the integers.

10
00:00:36,992 --> 00:00:42,417
On the number line, integers sit at evenly
spaced marks, stretching forever in both

11
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:43,136
directions.

12
00:00:44,267 --> 00:00:48,939
But there are numbers between the marks,
like one half, or negative three fourths.

13
00:00:49,389 --> 00:00:54,249
Any number that can be written as a
fraction, one integer over another,

14
00:00:54,249 --> 00:00:56,919
non-zero integer, is a rational number.

15
00:00:57,369 --> 00:01:02,724
Every integer is rational too, because
five, for example, equals five over one.

16
00:01:03,867 --> 00:01:06,683
Rational numbers also show up as decimals.

17
00:01:07,133 --> 00:01:12,167
Their decimals either stop, like zero
point seven five, which is three fourths,

18
00:01:12,617 --> 00:01:18,298
or repeat forever in a pattern, like zero
point three three three, and so on, which

19
00:01:18,298 --> 00:01:19,188
is one third.

20
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:24,869
Some numbers can't be written as a
fraction at all. Their decimals go on

21
00:01:24,869 --> 00:01:27,011
forever with no repeating pattern.

22
00:01:27,461 --> 00:01:31,813
These are irrational numbers. The square
root of two is one. So is pi.

23
00:01:32,263 --> 00:01:37,952
They still have exact spots on the number
line. The square root of two is about one

24
00:01:37,952 --> 00:01:41,585
point four one, and pi is about three
point one four.

25
00:01:42,733 --> 00:01:47,448
Put the rational and irrational numbers
together, and you get the real numbers.

26
00:01:47,898 --> 00:01:52,992
Here's the whole family. Natural numbers
sit inside the whole numbers, which sit

27
00:01:52,992 --> 00:01:56,303
inside the integers, which sit inside the
rationals.

28
00:01:56,753 --> 00:02:01,800
The irrationals sit beside the rationals,
and together they fill the entire number

29
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:02,108
line.

30
00:02:03,233 --> 00:02:08,393
The number line also lets us compare
numbers. A number to the right is always

31
00:02:08,393 --> 00:02:08,929
greater.

32
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:14,393
So negative two is greater than negative
five, even though five looks bigger.

33
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:19,856
Negative two is to the right, so negative
two is greater than negative five.

34
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,616
Your turn. Classify each number: negative
four, the square root of nine, two thirds,

35
00:02:26,616 --> 00:02:28,488
and the square root of five.

36
00:02:28,938 --> 00:02:32,927
Pause the video, and decide which families
each one belongs to.

37
00:02:33,377 --> 00:02:37,431
Negative four is an integer, so it's also
rational and real.

38
00:02:37,881 --> 00:02:43,289
The square root of nine equals three, so
it's natural, whole, an integer, rational,

39
00:02:43,289 --> 00:02:43,875
and real.

40
00:02:44,325 --> 00:02:49,518
Two thirds is rational and real. And the
square root of five is irrational and

41
00:02:49,518 --> 00:02:49,851
real.

42
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
If this helped, subscribe to School Math,
Explained, and turn on notifications so

43
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,984
What is three plus four times two?

44
00:02:53,434 --> 00:02:58,639
If you said fourteen, you added first. If
you said eleven, you multiplied first.

45
00:02:59,089 --> 00:03:03,567
Only one of those can be right, and in
this lesson we'll learn the rule that

46
00:03:03,567 --> 00:03:04,039
decides.

47
00:03:05,167 --> 00:03:10,514
Mathematicians agree on an order of
operations, so that every expression has

48
00:03:10,514 --> 00:03:11,780
exactly one value.

49
00:03:12,230 --> 00:03:14,705
First, grouping symbols, like parentheses.

50
00:03:15,155 --> 00:03:16,456
Second, exponents.

51
00:03:16,906 --> 00:03:20,682
Third, multiplication and division,
working from left to right.

52
00:03:21,132 --> 00:03:24,716
Fourth, addition and subtraction, also
from left to right.

53
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:28,820
Back to our question. Three plus four
times two.

54
00:03:29,270 --> 00:03:33,515
Multiplication comes before addition, so
four times two is eight.

55
00:03:33,965 --> 00:03:37,336
Then three plus eight is eleven. The
answer is eleven.

56
00:03:38,467 --> 00:03:43,858
Multiplication and division are partners.
Neither one always goes first. You just

57
00:03:43,858 --> 00:03:45,123
work left to right.

58
00:03:45,573 --> 00:03:50,863
In twelve divided by three, times two, we
divide first, because it's on the left.

59
00:03:51,313 --> 00:03:55,260
Twelve divided by three is four, and four
times two is eight.

60
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,896
The same goes for addition and
subtraction.

61
00:03:59,346 --> 00:04:03,591
Ten minus four plus three: subtract first,
because it's on the left.

62
00:04:04,041 --> 00:04:08,329
Ten minus four is six, and six plus three
is nine. Not three!

63
00:04:09,467 --> 00:04:14,966
Let's try a longer one: two times, open
parenthesis, five minus three, close

64
00:04:14,966 --> 00:04:18,512
parenthesis, squared, plus eight divided
by four.

65
00:04:18,962 --> 00:04:21,842
Parentheses first: five minus three is
two.

66
00:04:22,292 --> 00:04:24,660
Exponents next: two squared is four.

67
00:04:25,110 --> 00:04:30,881
Now multiply and divide, left to right:
two times four is eight, and eight divided

68
00:04:30,881 --> 00:04:31,937
by four is two.

69
00:04:32,387 --> 00:04:34,541
Finally, add: eight plus two is ten.

70
00:04:35,667 --> 00:04:41,249
One more thing about exponents. Negative
three squared, with no parentheses, means

71
00:04:41,249 --> 00:04:44,925
the negative of three squared, which is
negative nine.

72
00:04:45,375 --> 00:04:50,225
But negative three in parentheses,
squared, means negative three times

73
00:04:50,225 --> 00:04:52,927
negative three, which is positive nine.

74
00:04:53,377 --> 00:04:56,215
Parentheses tell you exactly what gets
squared.

75
00:04:57,333 --> 00:05:02,475
Your turn. Simplify: eighteen minus six
divided by three, plus two cubed.

76
00:05:02,925 --> 00:05:04,461
Pause the video and try it.

77
00:05:04,911 --> 00:05:07,087
Exponents first: two cubed is eight.

78
00:05:07,537 --> 00:05:10,502
Then division: six divided by three is
two.

79
00:05:10,952 --> 00:05:16,324
Now, left to right: eighteen minus two is
sixteen, and sixteen plus eight is twenty

80
00:05:16,324 --> 00:05:16,648
four.

81
00:05:17,766 --> 00:05:22,907
Algebra starts with one simple idea: using
a letter to stand for a number.

82
00:05:23,357 --> 00:05:28,409
In this lesson, we'll learn what variables
and expressions are, and how to evaluate

83
00:05:28,409 --> 00:05:31,635
an expression when we know the value of
its variable.

84
00:05:31,766 --> 00:05:38,364
A variable is a letter, like x, n, or t,
that represents a number we don't know

85
00:05:38,364 --> 00:05:40,702
yet, or a number that can change.

86
00:05:41,152 --> 00:05:46,982
For example, if a movie ticket costs eight
dollars, then n tickets cost eight times n

87
00:05:46,982 --> 00:05:47,531
dollars.

88
00:05:47,981 --> 00:05:50,711
As n changes, the total changes with it.

89
00:05:51,833 --> 00:05:57,906
An algebraic expression combines numbers,
variables, and operations. Three x plus

90
00:05:57,906 --> 00:05:59,555
five is an expression.

91
00:06:00,005 --> 00:06:05,864
Its parts separated by plus or minus signs
are called terms. Here, the terms are

92
00:06:05,864 --> 00:06:07,109
three x and five.

93
00:06:07,559 --> 00:06:13,226
The number multiplying a variable is its
coefficient, so three is the coefficient

94
00:06:13,226 --> 00:06:13,575
of x.

95
00:06:14,025 --> 00:06:17,631
A term with no variable, like five, is
called a constant.

96
00:06:18,766 --> 00:06:21,625
An expression is not the same as an
equation.

97
00:06:22,075 --> 00:06:27,865
An equation has an equal sign and states
that two things are equal, like three x

98
00:06:27,865 --> 00:06:29,819
plus five equals seventeen.

99
00:06:30,269 --> 00:06:35,520
An expression is just a value we can
calculate. We simplify or evaluate

100
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,183
expressions, and we solve equations.

101
00:06:39,333 --> 00:06:44,709
To evaluate an expression, substitute the
value of the variable, then follow the

102
00:06:44,709 --> 00:06:46,053
order of operations.

103
00:06:46,503 --> 00:06:50,087
Let's evaluate three x plus five when x
equals four.

104
00:06:50,537 --> 00:06:53,801
Replace x with four: three times four,
plus five.

105
00:06:54,251 --> 00:06:58,133
Multiply first, to get twelve plus five,
which is seventeen.

106
00:06:59,266 --> 00:07:04,817
Now an expression with two variables: two
a squared, minus b, when a equals three

107
00:07:04,817 --> 00:07:06,050
and b equals five.

108
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:09,572
Substitute: two times three squared, minus
five.

109
00:07:10,022 --> 00:07:14,545
Exponent first: three squared is nine.
Then two times nine is eighteen.

110
00:07:14,995 --> 00:07:17,107
And eighteen minus five is thirteen.

111
00:07:18,233 --> 00:07:21,113
We can also translate words into
expressions.

112
00:07:21,563 --> 00:07:27,268
Five more than twice a number. Let n be
the number. Twice the number is two n, and

113
00:07:27,268 --> 00:07:29,008
five more means add five.

114
00:07:29,458 --> 00:07:31,890
So the expression is two n plus five.

115
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:38,106
Watch out for phrases like three less than
a number. That's n minus three, not three

116
00:07:38,106 --> 00:07:38,655
minus n.

117
00:07:39,799 --> 00:07:45,794
Your turn. Evaluate x squared, minus four
x, plus one, when x equals negative two.

118
00:07:46,244 --> 00:07:50,105
Pause the video and try it. Be careful
with the negative sign.

119
00:07:50,555 --> 00:07:56,516
Substitute, using parentheses: negative
two in parentheses, squared, minus four

120
00:07:56,516 --> 00:07:58,705
times negative two, plus one.

121
00:07:59,155 --> 00:08:04,651
Negative two squared is positive four.
Minus four times negative two is plus

122
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:05,085
eight.

123
00:08:05,535 --> 00:08:08,714
So we get four plus eight plus one, which
is thirteen.

124
00:08:09,833 --> 00:08:14,206
Why can you add numbers in any order, but
not subtract them in any order?

125
00:08:14,656 --> 00:08:19,411
The answer comes from a handful of
properties that every number follows. In

126
00:08:19,411 --> 00:08:23,531
this lesson, we'll meet them, and see why
they make algebra work.

127
00:08:24,666 --> 00:08:28,549
First, the commutative property. Commute
means to move around.

128
00:08:28,999 --> 00:08:34,604
For addition, a plus b equals b plus a.
For example, three plus five and five plus

129
00:08:34,604 --> 00:08:36,039
three are both eight.

130
00:08:36,489 --> 00:08:40,009
For multiplication, a times b equals b
times a.

131
00:08:40,459 --> 00:08:46,343
But subtraction is not commutative. Five
minus three is two, while three minus five

132
00:08:46,343 --> 00:08:47,478
is negative two.

133
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:51,714
Next, the associative property. It's about
grouping.

134
00:08:52,164 --> 00:08:57,884
When you add three numbers, it doesn't
matter which pair you add first. a plus b,

135
00:08:57,884 --> 00:09:00,143
plus c, equals a, plus b plus c.

136
00:09:00,593 --> 00:09:07,045
The same is true for multiplication. Two
times five, times seven, equals two, times

137
00:09:07,045 --> 00:09:09,766
five times seven. Both are seventy.

138
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:15,252
The most important one in algebra is the
distributive property.

139
00:09:15,702 --> 00:09:21,959
a times the quantity b plus c equals a b
plus a c. The a gets multiplied by each

140
00:09:21,959 --> 00:09:24,150
term inside the parentheses.

141
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:30,323
Think of a rectangle that's three wide,
and x plus four long. Its area is three x

142
00:09:30,323 --> 00:09:31,170
plus twelve.

143
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:36,292
So three times the quantity x plus four
equals three x plus twelve.

144
00:09:37,433 --> 00:09:41,273
The distributive property also makes
mental math easier.

145
00:09:41,723 --> 00:09:47,378
Seven times ninety eight is the same as
seven times the quantity one hundred minus

146
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:47,654
two.

147
00:09:48,104 --> 00:09:52,306
That's seven hundred minus fourteen, which
is six hundred eighty six.

148
00:09:53,433 --> 00:09:55,609
Finally, identities and inverses.

149
00:09:56,059 --> 00:10:02,427
Adding zero leaves a number unchanged, so
zero is the additive identity. Multiplying

150
00:10:02,427 --> 00:10:07,430
by one leaves it unchanged, so one is the
multiplicative identity.

151
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:12,699
Every number has an opposite. a plus
negative a equals zero. That's the

152
00:10:12,699 --> 00:10:13,853
additive inverse.

153
00:10:14,303 --> 00:10:19,690
And every number except zero has a
reciprocal. a times one over a equals one.

154
00:10:19,690 --> 00:10:22,068
That's the multiplicative inverse.

155
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:25,952
Your turn. Name the property shown in each
line.

156
00:10:26,402 --> 00:10:33,092
Four times the quantity x minus two equals
four x minus eight. Six plus negative six

157
00:10:33,092 --> 00:10:39,543
equals zero. And two times five, times
seven, equals two, times five times seven.

158
00:10:39,993 --> 00:10:41,614
Pause the video and decide.

159
00:10:42,064 --> 00:10:47,583
The first is the distributive property.
The second is the additive inverse. The

160
00:10:47,583 --> 00:10:51,216
third is the associative property of
multiplication.

161
00:10:52,366 --> 00:10:55,182
Long expressions can often be made much
shorter.

162
00:10:55,632 --> 00:11:00,744
In this lesson, we'll learn to spot like
terms, and combine them to simplify an

163
00:11:00,744 --> 00:11:01,456
expression.

164
00:11:02,599 --> 00:11:07,207
Like terms have exactly the same variable
part, with the same exponents.

165
00:11:07,657 --> 00:11:13,235
Three x and five x are like terms. So are
two y squared and negative seven y

166
00:11:13,235 --> 00:11:13,823
squared.

167
00:11:14,273 --> 00:11:19,163
But three x and three x squared are not
like terms, because the exponents are

168
00:11:19,163 --> 00:11:19,798
different.

169
00:11:20,248 --> 00:11:25,305
And four y and four are not like terms
either, because one has a variable and the

170
00:11:25,305 --> 00:11:26,179
other doesn't.

171
00:11:27,299 --> 00:11:32,710
To combine like terms, add or subtract
their coefficients, and keep the variable

172
00:11:32,710 --> 00:11:33,657
part the same.

173
00:11:34,107 --> 00:11:36,368
Three x plus five x is eight x.

174
00:11:36,818 --> 00:11:42,234
This works because of the distributive
property: three x plus five x equals the

175
00:11:42,234 --> 00:11:45,799
quantity three plus five, times x, which
is eight x.

176
00:11:46,249 --> 00:11:51,252
Think of it like three apples plus five
apples. You get eight apples, not eight

177
00:11:51,252 --> 00:11:52,201
apples squared.

178
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:58,069
Let's simplify seven a, plus two b, minus
three a, plus six b.

179
00:11:58,519 --> 00:12:03,809
First, group the like terms. Seven a minus
three a, and two b plus six b.

180
00:12:04,259 --> 00:12:08,931
Seven a minus three a is four a. Two b
plus six b is eight b.

181
00:12:09,381 --> 00:12:14,382
So the expression simplifies to four a
plus eight b. We can't combine those,

182
00:12:14,382 --> 00:12:16,421
because they're not like terms.

183
00:12:17,566 --> 00:12:19,849
Sometimes you need to distribute first.

184
00:12:20,299 --> 00:12:24,480
Simplify two times the quantity x plus
three, plus four x.

185
00:12:24,930 --> 00:12:28,237
Distribute the two: two x plus six, plus
four x.

186
00:12:28,687 --> 00:12:32,697
Now combine two x and four x, to get six x
plus six.

187
00:12:33,833 --> 00:12:37,097
Be careful with a minus sign in front of
parentheses.

188
00:12:37,547 --> 00:12:43,882
In five x minus the quantity two x minus
four, the minus sign applies to every term

189
00:12:43,882 --> 00:12:44,416
inside.

190
00:12:44,866 --> 00:12:51,086
It becomes five x minus two x plus four.
Notice the minus four turned into plus

191
00:12:51,086 --> 00:12:51,479
four.

192
00:12:51,929 --> 00:12:54,233
Combining, we get three x plus four.

193
00:12:54,366 --> 00:13:01,134
Your turn. Simplify three times the
quantity two y minus one, minus y, plus

194
00:13:01,134 --> 00:13:01,595
seven.

195
00:13:02,045 --> 00:13:03,581
Pause the video and try it.

196
00:13:04,031 --> 00:13:08,341
Distribute the three: six y minus three,
minus y, plus seven.

197
00:13:08,791 --> 00:13:15,509
Combine the y terms: six y minus y is five
y. Combine the constants: negative three

198
00:13:15,509 --> 00:13:17,047
plus seven is four.

199
00:13:17,497 --> 00:13:19,630
The answer is five y plus four.

200
00:13:20,766 --> 00:13:25,807
That completes Unit One. Next, we'll start
solving equations. If this helped,

201
00:13:25,807 --> 00:13:31,044
subscribe to School Math, Explained, and
turn on notifications so you don't miss

202
00:13:31,044 --> 00:13:32,222
it. See you there.

